-- =====================================================================
-- AEGIS-EBS demo seed dataset — ALIGNED WITH THE SERVER DEMO WORLD.
--
-- Source of truth: aegis-server ServerStore.seedWorld (run by ServerMain
-- on startup unless --no-seed). This file mirrors that world EXACTLY:
--   building  : id AEGIS-BLD-A, code A, "AEGIS Tower A"
--   topology  : 10 floors x 4 zones (F01-A..F10-D) x 12 devices = 480
--   devices   : DEV-A-F{nn}-{A..D}-{01..12} (ServerConfig devicesPerZone=12)
--   users     : admin (SYSTEM_ADMIN), secops (SECURITY_OPERATOR),
--               floor7 (FLOOR_MANAGER), employee (EMPLOYEE)
--   grants    : secops -> building-wide PUBLISH; floor7 -> floor 7 PUBLISH
--               (SYSTEM_ADMIN publishes anywhere via ScopedRBAC; no grant row)
-- Additions beyond seedWorld (showcase only): zone display_x/display_y grid,
-- FIRE/DRILL alert_templates (vi/en), FIRE_DRILL demo_scenarios row.
--
-- TWO MODES — DO NOT MIX THEM ON ONE DB:
--   MODE 1 (live demo, recommended): scripts/initdb.sh then start ServerMain.
--     The server seeds this same world itself WITH REAL Argon2id hashes:
--     logins admin/admin-demo-secret, secops/secops-demo-secret,
--     floor7/floor7-demo-secret, employee/employee-demo-secret;
--     device credential device-demo-secret (shared fleet hash, lab only).
--     Do NOT apply this file to that DB: seedWorld is idempotent and SKIPS
--     when building AEGIS-BLD-A already exists — the placeholder hashes
--     below would then block ALL authentication.
--   MODE 2 (offline dataset): scripts/initdb.sh <file> then apply this file
--     to inspect the demo world (ERD/dashboard mock/SQL). Hashes are
--     PLACEHOLDERS: authentication fails until they are replaced with
--     PasswordHasher (Argon2id) output. See docs/BUILD.md for the verified
--     hash-generation recipe (jshell) and simulator fleet registration.
--
-- Apply ONCE after 001_base_schema.sql + 002_showcase_expansion.sql.
-- Plain INSERTs: re-running on a seeded DB fails on PRIMARY KEY/UNIQUE by
-- design. No transaction statements here (if ever loaded via
-- MigrationRunner it wraps the script in BEGIN IMMEDIATE itself).
-- The leading PRAGMA enables FK enforcement for the sqlite3 CLI path
-- (CLI defaults foreign_keys=OFF); inside a transaction it is a no-op —
-- the authoritative source there is Db.open() (PRAGMA foreign_keys=ON).
--
-- SECURITY NOTE: every password_hash / credential_hash below is an
-- explicit PLACEHOLDER, not a real Argon2id hash and not a real secret.
-- Demo logins/device auth will fail until they are replaced with hashes
-- produced by PasswordHasher. Never commit real credentials to this file.
--
-- All ids are deterministic UUIDv5 (namespace: DNS "aegis-ebs.demo.seed"),
-- except buildings.id which is the literal ServerConfig default buildingId.
-- Timestamps are fixed-width UTC ISO-8601 with 9 nano digits (Sql.TS format)
-- so TEXT ordering stays chronological alongside server-written rows.
-- =====================================================================

PRAGMA foreign_keys=ON;

